  "step_3": "The decision reason involves comparing the maximum magnitude outcomes (2500€ vs 2400€) weighted by their probabilities. The individual considers the maximum magnitude outcomes (explicitly noting the 100€ difference) and acknowledges the small probability difference, but dismisses it as negligible. While the decision reason formally uses the weighted value (outcome × probability), the individual does not mention such a calculation. However, their focus on the higher outcome and de-emphasis on small probability differences aligns closely with the core logic of the reason—prioritizing the more favorable high outcome, especially when probability differences are small. Although the exact weighting is not mentioned, the qualitative reasoning is consistent with the decision reason’s preference structure. The individual’s emphasis on the larger amount and indifference to minor probability shifts suggests they are intuitively applying a similar rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
